# Swaying one body by hand
# A movement you can start from the control page on any single body - a male, a female,
# or the bar - without the rest of the artwork running. Useful for checking a motor, a
# travel range, or how long one sweep really takes. The artwork never does this on its
# own: when a body moves by itself it is because it is calling or looking, not because of
# this. Times are estimates - this is a good movement to time with a stopwatch.

0 You press start on that body's "turn back and forth" on the control page.
0 It sets off towards one end of its travel. For a male or a female that is about a quarter turn; for the bar it is its whole length.
6 It arrives - about 6 seconds for a body, about half a minute for the bar.
0 Without pausing, it sets off back towards the other end.
6 It arrives at the other end.
0 And so on, back and forth at the same speed, indefinitely, until you press stop.
0 No lights change while this runs, and no appetite is involved. A body swaying like this has nothing to do with whether it is hungry - it is just the motor moving.
